Always watch the tutubi... 

MA'AM SANTOS: In Science, we call that high humidity. When a really big rain is coming, the air gets packed with invisible water vapor. All that heavy moisture sticks to their tiny wings and weighs them down, you see? They get too heavy to fly high up in the clouds. So when you see them flying so low... it means they are panicking to find a hiding place before the storm hits!

Oh no... What if they can't find a place to hide under before the rain falls? 

Where will they go? 

